# Tor for net/ (vpn). Installed as /etc/tor/torrc by install.sh net,
# which keeps the User and DataDirectory lines of the torrc that was
# there. The vpn service starts Tor right after OpenVPN, so Tor always
# goes out through the VPN (straight out only in level 0 and the
# sandbox).

# --- SOCKS ports: each has its own circuits and exits, so sites can't
# link what goes through one port to what goes through another.

# proxychains run as proxychains4, or with -f (not our wrapper)
SocksPort 127.0.0.1:9050
# vpn's clock: each mirror on its own circuit (IsolateDestAddr), so one
# exit can't fake the time for both
SocksPort 127.0.0.1:9059 IsolateDestAddr
# browsers, one port each (set it as SOCKS5, DNS through the proxy)
# 9150 IceCat, 9151 Chromium, 9152 and 9153 any other
SocksPort 127.0.0.1:9150
SocksPort 127.0.0.1:9151
SocksPort 127.0.0.1:9152
SocksPort 127.0.0.1:9153
